Spec: ServiceDeleteCmd

Purpose:
  Back the `agent service delete` sub-command: resolve one @ServiceInstance by namespace
    and name, publish it as the process-wide owner context and as the Rhai variable
    `instance`, inject the parsed CLI flags as the Rhai variable `args`, then hand the
    whole delete work to the Rhai modules `context` and `delete`. This file runs no
    delete stage itself: no directory or resource teardown, no `status` write, no CR
    removal — it only prepares the engine and hands off. Near-twin of the
    `agent system delete` lane (./../system/delete.sdd), diff-verified to differ only at
    the kind segment (`{script_dir}/service` over `{script_dir}/system`, @set_service
    over @set_system, @ServiceInstance over @SystemInstance) and the two extra
    `-t`/`--template-dir` and `--agent-image` flags; the snippet, the remaining three
    search directories and the step order are identical.

References:
  ./../system/delete.sdd — the diff-verified near-twin; the cross-kind template-flag
    question is open there as a task and mirrored here.
  ./install.sdd — the sibling install lane, whose shape this file copies minus
    `--tag`: nine fields instead of ten, and the snippet imports `delete` where
    install imports `install`.
  ./mod.sdd — the frozen Delete dispatch arm bounding this lane's failures:
    `Deleting a package failed with: {e:}` then @process::exit(3).

Must:
  Execute these steps in this order, with nothing between them: build the interpreter,
    fetch the CR, publish context, inject `instance`, serialize and inject `args`,
    evaluate the snippet, return @Ok.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories in this
    order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the directory itself),
    `{script_dir}/service`, `{script_dir}/lib` — plain string interpolation of
    @std::path::Display, so a path argument ending in `/` doubles the separator;
    earlier entries win an `import`.
  @Script::new brings the full registration set — including @service_rhai_register, so
    the scripts hold `get_service_instance`, `list_services_names` and the whole
    @ServiceInstance bridge — plus http, s3, the other two instance kinds, the jukebox
    and the k8s registrars, the same set the install lane gets.
  Fetch the CR with @ServiceInstance::get taking clones of @Parameters.namespace and
    @Parameters.instance — one namespaced named-object read in the given namespace,
    never a list, watch, patch or delete; an absent instance is an @Err, not a
    bootstrap path.
  Publish the fetched CR twice from the fetched value and one clone: @set_service
    stores the clone as the process owner context, and @rhai::Scope::set_value on
    @Script::ctx moves the original into the script variable named `instance`.
  Serialize @Parameters with @serde_json::to_value and inject it through
    @Script::set_dynamic as the script variable named `args`; the JSON object carries
    the declared snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`, `vynil_namespace`,
    `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`, `config_dir`,
    `controller_values` — nine keys, no `tag` — `controller_values` as a JSON string
    (its default renders `"{}"`, still a string, not an object), `agent_image` as a
    string and the @PathBufs as path text.
  Evaluate the fixed four-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it:
    `import("context") as ctx;` then `let context = ctx::run(instance, args);` then
    `import("delete") as delete;` then `delete::run(instance, context);` — the
    `context` script runs first, its returned value becoming the `delete::run` second
    argument; `delete` runs second and last; the final statement ends with `;` so the
    resulting @rhai::Dynamic::UNIT is discarded by `let _ =` while a failed evaluation
    still propagates through `?`.
  Import lazily per statement as @rhai does: the `delete` module is only resolved when
    its `import` statement executes, so a missing `delete` module fails the eval only
    after `ctx::run` side effects have already run.
  Perform no cluster mutation of its own: every teardown and `status` write happens
    inside the Rhai modules through the registered @ServiceInstance bridge; this file
    only reads the CR.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Treat an absent or already-deleted @ServiceInstance as success: the `NotFound` from
    @ServiceInstance::get must propagate as a failure into the exit(3) lane — the fetch
    precedes any handoff, so absence tolerance cannot be assumed.
  Close out the delete in Rust: remove the @ServiceInstance CR, add a finalizer, write
    a `status`, or delete anything under @Parameters.package_dir from this lane — even
    after the snippet succeeded; teardown and file removal belong to the scripts and
    the controller, not to this handoff file.
  Read `template_dir` or `agent_image` to steer this lane: those service-only flags
    reach the scripts only through `args`, and consuming them here would move
    script-side work into the handoff.
  Interpret `controller_values` or gate on its contents.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver semantics and registration set,
    @Script::eval error lane, @Script::set_dynamic, @Script::ctx.
  /common/src/instanceservice.sdd — @ServiceInstance and the @ServiceInstance::get
    lookup this file awaits (attached by @impl_instance_common! per
    /common/src/instance_macros.sdd), and the registered bridges the scripts use for
    teardown writes.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @set_service store semantics and runtime preconditions.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error variants, @common::Result and the
    @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE default of `agent_image`.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing (flags, envs, defaults below) and
    the derives behind the `args` JSON.
  /agent/scripts/service/context.rhai and /agent/scripts/service/delete.rhai — runtime
    handoff targets the snippet imports under the default `--script-dir`; owned instead
    by /agent/agent.sdd and unspecified here. The guarded stage dispatch (`delete_pre`,
    the `is_dir` and `tofu` re-checks over the `{package_dir}` stage directories) lives
    inside that `delete` module; this Rust file never names those stage modules.
  ./mod.rs — the only caller: @context::init_k8s call, then this arm's
    `unwrap_or_else` error lane (tracing text and @process::exit(3), frozen by
    ./mod.sdd).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct, also deriving @Debug, @Serialize and @Deserialize;
    mounted by @service::Commands::Delete in ./mod.rs; all nine fields private to this
    module, reached only by the derive code and by this file.
  @run — @pub async fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>; the sole
    caller is @service::run (delete dispatch arm).

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name
    `NAMESPACE`, @String, required (no `default_value`); the doc comment calls it the
    instance namespace to delete.
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name `INSTANCE`,
    @String, required; names the CR to fetch and is never validated here.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`,
    value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; never read in this file beyond
    serialization into `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `/tmp/package`.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/scripts`.
  @Parameters.template_dir — `-t` / `--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, value
    name `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/templates`; a
    service- and tenant-only flag absent from the system twin, read by nothing in this
    Rust lane.
  @Parameters.agent_image — long-only `--agent-image`, env `AGENT_IMAGE`, value name
    `AGENT_IMAGE`, @String, clap default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE, i.e.
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`; the other service-only flag of the twin.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name
    `CONFIG_DIR`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env
    `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default the
    two-character string `{}`.
  Shape delta vs ./install.sdd: no `tag` / `TAG` flag at all — nine fields, not ten;
    otherwise the flag, env and default spellings are install's verbatim.
  Implicit runtime precondition: a live tokio multi-thread runtime (from @main's
    @tokio::main), because @context::set_service crosses state with
    @tokio::task::block_in_place; @context::init_k8s already ran in @service::run
    before this file is entered and is inert either way.

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed eval snippet completes without a Rhai error — the @Dynamic
    value the snippet returns is discarded, never inspected.

Raises:
  @common::Error::KubeError from @ServiceInstance::get when the API server rejects the
    lookup — including `NotFound` for an already-gone instance (the whole @kube::Error
    is mapped, Display `K8s error: ...`, never defaulted); the first fallible step,
    nothing published to context or scripts when it fails.
  @common::Error::SerializationError from the explicit @map_err when
    @serde_json::to_value(@Parameters) fails on the derives.
  @common::Error::Core (wrapping @vynil_core::Error::RhaiError, Display
    `Rhai script error: <rhai text>`) from the `?` on @Script::eval — a parse error in
    the fixed snippet, a failed `context` or `delete` import, or any parse error /
    thrown error inside those modules and whatever they import_run.
  The context-owned @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` surfaces through
    @ServiceInstance::get via @get_client_async when no kubeconfig or in-cluster
    configuration resolves.
  Panics from @context::set_service on a current-thread runtime or no runtime at all
    (contract in /common/src/context.sdd), not catchable by the parent `?` lane.

Handles:
  @Err lane owned by the caller — @service::run logs `Deleting a package failed with:`
    followed by the error Display through @tracing::error and calls @process::exit(3);
    code `3` is this arm's delete-specific exit, shared with the system twin, distinct
    from install's `1`. This file logs nothing and never exits, so a failed delete
    leaves no status marker written by this lane.
  Failed lookup or failed eval after @set_service already ran — the process context
    keeps the @VynilContext::ServiceInstance variant for the remaining process lifetime
    (which ends in the exit(3)).
  Already-gone instance — no absence-tolerance branch: the hard @KubeError above is
    the whole behaviour; no script ever runs to do an idempotent no-op delete.
  Half-deleted instance — no branch on `status`, finalizers or the contents of
    @Parameters.package_dir here: a rerun refetches the CR and replays both modules;
    stage skipping (the `is_dir` and `tofu` guards) is `delete.rhai`'s script-side
    contract.
  Absent resolver directories — the four search paths are never existence-checked at
    construction; the failure only lands later as the @common::Error::Core import error
    if no search dir holds `context.rhai` / `delete.rhai`.
  Flags with no local reader (`vynil_namespace`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `controller_values`) — their only observable use is the `args` JSON the scripts
    consume; the `context` module picks up `template_dir` and `agent_image` from there.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover all six Scenarios with tests; no test invokes this @run —
      /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs exercises the service `context`/`delete` Rhai
      modules on a mock engine, bypassing this Rust lane.
  [?] Twin flag drift: this lane and /agent/src/tenant/delete.rs carry
      `-t`/`--template-dir` and `--agent-image` like their install twins, while
      /agent/src/system/delete.rs is exactly the seven-flag system shape minus
      `--tag`; apart from the kind segment the three copies are diff-verified
      identical. Cross-ref the open tasks in /agent/src/system/delete.sdd and
      ./install.sdd: decide whether the template flags belong to one shared shape or
      the system kind genuinely needs neither.
  [?] Delete of an already-gone instance is a hard failure: @ServiceInstance::get runs
      first, so a retried delete Job whose CR was removed meanwhile (controller
      cleanup, or an earlier partial run) exits 3 instead of converging silently.
      Same open point as /agent/src/system/delete.sdd: confirm the controller never
      re-dispatches this Job after the CR is gone, or decide whether `NotFound` on the
      delete lane becomes a silent @Ok.
  [?] `vynil_namespace`, `template_dir`, `agent_image` and `controller_values` are
      typed, required in `vynil_namespace`'s case, yet this lane never reads them —
      their contract lives only in the script-side `args` JSON. Same open point as
      ./install.sdd: confirm the requiredness belongs to the Rhai contract or relax
      the flags.
  [?] `controller_values` reaches scripts as a JSON string even when it holds `{}`,
      so every consumer must decode it. Decide whether this file should pre-parse it
      into an object (mirrors ./install.sdd and the system twin).
  [?] The eval @Dynamic is discarded (`let _ =`): confirm no `delete::run` return
      value may ever gate success, closing a delete Job that half-failed.
  [?] @Deserialize on @Parameters has no deserialization site in the workspace (the
      Rust lane only serializes it toward scripts). Decide whether the derive stays.

Done when:
  The six Scenarios hold under tests pinning resolver-path order, the nine-key `args`
    JSON with no `tag` and `template_dir`/`agent_image` present at their defaults and
    `controller_values` as a string, and the error-to-exit(3) lane including the
    already-gone-CR hard failure.

Scenario: full run hands off in order
  Given all required flags supplied (by flag or env), an existing namespaced
    @ServiceInstance named by @Parameters.instance, and `context.rhai` plus
    `delete.rhai` resolvable under `{script_dir}/service`
  When @run is awaited
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`, `[config]`,
    `[script]/service`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And before the eval, the process owner context is the service variant (via
    @set_service) and `instance` and `args` are bound, `args` carrying the nine
    snake_case keys with `controller_values` as a JSON string
  Then the `context` module's `run` executes before the `delete` module's `run`,
    receiving (`instance`, `args`), and the resulting `context` value is what
    `delete::run` receives
  And @run returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was, having performed no
    cluster write and no file deletion of its own

Scenario: service-only flags reach scripts at their defaults
  Given a command line that sets the required flags but omits `-t`/`--template-dir` and
    `--agent-image`
  When @run serializes @Parameters into `args`
  Then the object holds exactly the nine keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `config_dir`, `controller_values` — no `tag` key
  And `template_dir` is `./agent/templates`, `agent_image` is
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7` and `controller_values` is the JSON string `"{}"`

Scenario: absent or already-gone CR fails before any handoff
  Given no @ServiceInstance exists at that namespace/name — never created, or removed
    by an earlier delete run or by the controller
  When @run is awaited
  Then the @ServiceInstance::get `?` returns @Err(@common::Error::KubeError)
  And @set_service never ran (context stays @VynilContext::None), `instance`/`args`
    were never injected and neither module ran
  And @service::run logs `Deleting a package failed with: K8s error: ...` at
    @tracing::error level and exits the process 3

Scenario: missing required flag never reaches Rust logic
  Given `--instance` omitted and `INSTANCE` unset in the environment — same lane for
    `--namespace` / `NAMESPACE` and `--vynil-namespace` / `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`
  When the binary parses @Parameters
  Then clap exits with its usage error before @run starts — no interpreter, no cluster
    read, and the exit-3 delete lane is never entered

Scenario: delete module missing after context already ran
  Given a valid @ServiceInstance, `context.rhai` resolvable in a search dir, and no
    `delete.rhai` resolvable in any of the four resolver directories
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then `ctx::run` and its side effects execute first, then @Script::eval returns
    @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed `Rhai script error:`)
  And the process context still holds the service variant when the exit(3) lane fires

Scenario: rerun over a half-deleted instance
  Given a @ServiceInstance whose `{package_dir}` stage content was already torn down by
    a previous delete run
  When @run is invoked again with the same flags
  Then the CR is refetched and both modules replay from the top — this file skips
    nothing based on `status` or on the stage directories, whose re-check is
    `delete.rhai`'s script-side contract
